<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akmal Ikramov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1898">1898</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akmal Ikramov was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> communist leader, first secretary of the Communist Party of the Uzbek SSR from 1929 to 1937. He oversaw collectivisation and the expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> growing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>. Arrested in Stalin's purges in 1937, he was tried with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolai-bukharin">Nikolai Bukharin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fayzulla-khodzhayev">Fayzulla Khodzhayev</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> show trial of 1938 and shot.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akmal-ikramov.jpg" alt="Akmal Ikramov" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akmal_Ikramov_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
